Package: enigma2-plugin-extensions-unifi-protect-display
Version: 0.8.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: empyfi
Section: extra
Priority: optional
License: GPL-2.0-or-later
Depends: enigma2
Recommends: ffmpeg, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good-rtsp, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good-rtpmanager
Source: https://github.com/empyfi/UniFiProtectDisplay
Description: Show UniFi Protect cameras on your receiver
 Puts UniFi Protect cameras in the receiver's channel list as ordinary
 channels, one per camera, plus entries showing every camera at once and
 playing them in turn. They can also be shown in a corner of the screen
 over live television, or full screen. Cameras are discovered through the
 Protect Integration API, which also enables each camera's RTSP stream,
 so no stream URLs have to be copied by hand.
 .
 The corner offers two modes. Snapshots work on every receiver and need
 no extra packages. Live video uses the PiP decoder together with
 ffmpeg, which remuxes RTSP into MPEG-TS; it needs a box with a second
 video decoder and the ffmpeg package. The plugin detects which modes
 the box supports and says why one is unavailable.
